; 12-write-and-load-a-reusable-theory.kurt
;
; Write and load a reusable theory
;
; A theory is an ordinary `.kurt` file. Facts cross a `load` boundary only when they have a label
; and are not marked `local`.
;
; The theory of this lesson is the file `my-theory.kurt` next to this one:
;
;     load prop
;     bool P, Q
;
;     use P implies Q  "P-to-Q"
;     use P            "P"
;     use Q local      "internal-helper"
;
; This file uses it:

load my-theory

P
P implies Q
Q

; The labelled facts `P` and `P implies Q` are exported. The `local` fact stays inside
; `my-theory.kurt`. Unlabelled facts also stay local. A symbol declaration travels with an
; exported fact when that fact needs it; there is no separate export declaration.
;
; Give labels stable, descriptive names. They appear in proof reasons and make exported theory
; APIs clearer.
